 "unread": [
  "CKD. signature in the title block is illegible",
  "Hand-written pencil note near the title block (around 'T-16 ... Pad 14 ... Pad 8db ... Direct inpt 4-0') is only partly legible; values of the sketched resistors read as 240, 240 and 150 (or 15) ohms"
 ],
 "confidence": "high",
 "notes": "Single 22-way edge connector, rear view; the drawing does not name it (file name 'P16' is taken as a page number, so it is called P1 here). Letters A-Z (no G, I, O, Q) and numbers 1-22 are opposite contacts of the same row, each labelled separately, so each is its own pin entry. Every output is labelled identically on its letter and number contact (e.g. N and 12 both '-70 dBm 150Ω'): read as a balanced pair, but the drawing marks no +/- polarity, so ports use 'a' (letter side) / 'b' (number side) and polarity is null. Outputs grouped by bracket as DIRECT OUTPUT (N/12, P/13, R/14) and SWITCHED OUTPUT (S/15, T/16, U/17 NC, V/18 CTL). CTL taken as the control line that switches the SWITCHED OUTPUT; its direction is not drawn. Power only on the number side: 19 -25V, 20 COM, 21 +25V, 22 CHASSIS; W, X, Y, Z NC. Legend: NC = NOT CONNECTED. Title block: Ward-Beck Systems Ltd., M452 Oscillator Module Connector Rear View, 452-04-002, size A, iss. 2, drn. G.R., date Sept 77, ckd. initials (illegible signature). Hand-written pencil mods on this copy: a resistor sketched across L-10 labelled '150Ω' (or '15Ω'), resistors labelled '240' on each side running down to N/12, S/15 circled, and a note near the title block reading roughly 'T-16 - Pad 14 ... Pad 8db ... Direct inpt 4-0' (partly illegible)."
}